Course.start({"num":12,"unit":3,"slug":"m12-verbos-er-ir","minutes":45,"title":"Los verbos -er e -ir","subtitle":"Regular -er and -ir verbs in the present tense","lede":"The other two verb families work just like -ar verbs, with different vowels. And -er and -ir verbs are twins: they share all but two endings.","recap":"Last time you learned the -ar endings: **-o, -as, -a, -amos, -áis, -an** (*hablo, hablas, habla…*).","context":{"title":"Un caballero que lee demasiado","place":"La Mancha, España","text":"In **1605**, **Miguel de Cervantes** published the first part of **Don Quijote de la Mancha**, often called the first modern novel. Its hero is a man from La Mancha who **reads** so many old stories about knights that he decides to become one himself.\n\nHe puts on rusty armor, names his skinny horse Rocinante, and rides out to fight giants. The giants are really windmills. His neighbor Sancho Panza, a practical farmer, comes along as his squire and tries to keep him out of trouble.\n\nThe book has been translated into more languages than almost any book except the Bible. Its first line is famous across the Spanish-speaking world: {{En un lugar de la Mancha, de cuyo nombre no quiero acordarme…}} (*In a village of La Mancha, whose name I do not care to remember…*). Today we say {{Don Quijote lee libros y vive aventuras.}}"},"learn":[{"title":"Same idea, new endings","text":"Take off **-er** or **-ir**, then add the endings. Compare the two tables: they differ only in the **nosotros** and **vosotros** forms.","conj":[{"inf":"comer","en":"to eat","forms":["com**o**","com**es**","com**e**","com**emos**","com**éis**","com**en**"]},{"inf":"vivir","en":"to live","forms":["viv**o**","viv**es**","viv**e**","viv**imos**","viv**ís**","viv**en**"]}],"tip":"The **yo** form always ends in **-o**, in all three families: *hablo, como, vivo*."},{"title":"Common -er and -ir verbs","flash":[["aprender","to learn"],["beber","to drink"],["comprender","to understand"],["correr","to run"],["creer","to believe, to think"],["deber","should, must"],["leer","to read"],["vender","to sell"],["abrir","to open"],["compartir","to share"],["escribir","to write"],["recibir","to receive"],["asistir a","to attend"],["decidir","to decide"]]},{"title":"Verbs that bring a friend","text":"Some verbs are often followed by an infinitive or a small word:","examples":[["Debo estudiar más.","I should study more."],["Aprendemos a tocar el piano.","We're learning to play the piano."],["Asisto a una escuela católica.","I attend a Catholic school."],["Creo que sí.","I think so."],["¿Comprendes la pregunta?","Do you understand the question?"]],"tip":"**Aprender a** + infinitive: *aprendo **a** nadar*. **Asistir a** + place: *asisto **a** clase*. **Deber** + infinitive needs no extra word: *debes leer*."}],"tasks":[{"id":"t1","type":"conj","title":"Conjugate one of each","intro":"Write all the forms. Watch the nosotros and vosotros forms.","verbs":[{"inf":"correr","en":"to run","forms":["corro","corres","corre","corremos","corréis","corren"]},{"inf":"escribir","en":"to write","forms":["escribo","escribes","escribe","escribimos","escribís","escriben"]}],"hints":["-er: **-o, -es, -e, -emos, -éis, -en**.","-ir: **-o, -es, -e, -imos, -ís, -en**."]},{"id":"t2","type":"sort","title":"-er or -ir?","intro":"The nosotros form shows the verb family. Is each verb an -er or an -ir verb?","cats":["-er","-ir"],"speak":true,"items":[["comemos",0],["vivimos",1],["leemos",0],["escribimos",1],["bebemos",0],["abrimos",1],["corremos",0],["recibimos",1],["compartimos",1],["aprendemos",0]],"hints":["**-emos** comes from an -er verb; **-imos** from an -ir verb."]},{"id":"t3","type":"select","title":"Choose the right form","intro":"Tap the verb that matches the subject.","items":[{"s":"Yo {leo|lee|lees} un libro de Cervantes."},{"s":"Mi hermano {bebe|bebes|beben} mucha agua."},{"s":"Nosotros {vivimos|vivemos|viven} en Scranton."},{"s":"¿Tú {comprendes|comprende|comprendo} la lección?"},{"s":"Mis abuelos {venden|vende|vendemos} fruta en el mercado."},{"s":"Mis amigos y yo {compartimos|compartemos|comparten} la pizza."},{"s":"Vosotros {escribís|escribéis|escriben} muchos correos."},{"s":"Usted {debe|debes|deben} descansar."}],"hints":["*-ir* verbs use **-imos** and **-ís**; *-er* verbs use **-emos** and **-éis**."]},{"id":"t4","type":"cloze","title":"Complete the sentences","intro":"Write the correct form of the verb in parentheses.","pick":8,"items":["Don Quijote [lee] ((leer)) muchos libros.","Yo [escribo] ((escribir)) en mi cuaderno.","Nosotros [aprendemos] ((aprender)) español.","¿Dónde [vives] ((vivir)) tú?","Ellos [corren] ((correr)) en el parque.","La tienda [abre] ((abrir)) a las nueve.","Tú y yo [recibimos] ((recibir)) buenas notas.","Mis padres [creen] ((creer)) en mí.","Vosotros [bebéis] ((beber)) café con leche.","Ustedes [asisten] ((asistir)) a la misa los domingos."],"hints":["*Tú y yo* = nosotros.","*-ir* verbs: **-imos**. *-er* verbs: **-emos**.","Vosotros: **-éis** (-er) or **-ís** (-ir), with an accent."]},{"id":"t5","type":"sort","title":"¿Cierto o falso?","intro":"Read and listen to Pablo's description, then decide if each sentence is true (cierto) or false (falso).","passage":"{{Me llamo Pablo y vivo en Toledo, una ciudad cerca de Madrid.}} {{Asisto a un colegio grande.}} {{Por la mañana corro en el parque con mi perro.}} {{En la escuela aprendemos inglés y francés.}} {{Mi amiga Lucía escribe poemas y lee mucho.}} {{Por la tarde, mis amigos y yo comemos en una cafetería y compartimos una pizza.}} {{No bebo refrescos; bebo agua.}}","cats":["Cierto","Falso"],"items":[["Pablo vive en Madrid.",1,"He lives in Toledo, *near* Madrid."],["Pablo corre por la mañana.",0],["En su escuela aprenden alemán.",1,"They learn English and French."],["Lucía escribe poemas.",0],["Pablo y sus amigos comparten una pizza.",0],["Pablo bebe muchos refrescos.",1,"*No bebo refrescos.*"]],"hints":["Find the verb in each sentence, then look for the same verb in the text."]},{"id":"t6","type":"dictation","title":"Listen and write","intro":"Write each sentence you hear.","pick":4,"items":["Vivimos en una casa pequeña.","¿Qué lees?","Debo escribir la tarea.","Mi madre vende libros.","Comprendo un poco.","Ellos abren la puerta."],"hints":["Listen to the end of each verb to know who's doing it."]},{"id":"s1","type":"speak","title":"Say it out loud","intro":"Listen, record, compare.","items":[{"s":"En un lugar de la Mancha, de cuyo nombre no quiero acordarme."},{"s":"Leo, escribo y aprendo."}]}],"build":{"heading":"Leo, escribo, vivo","prompt":"Write **at least 5 sentences** about what you, your family and friends do. Use at least **five different -er or -ir verbs**, including at least one **nosotros** form (*-emos* or *-imos*).","model":"{{Vivo en Dunmore con mi familia.}} {{Asisto a una escuela grande.}} {{Por la mañana bebo jugo de naranja.}} {{Mi hermana lee libros de fantasía.}} {{Mis amigos y yo corremos en el parque.}} {{Mis padres comen a las seis.}}","placeholder":"Vivo en…","reqs":[{"t":"At least 5 sentences","sentences":5},{"t":"Five different -er / -ir verbs","min":5,"any":["como","comes","come","comemos","coméis","comen","vivo","vives","vive","vivimos","vivís","viven","aprendo","aprendes","aprende","aprendemos","aprenden","bebo","bebes","bebe","bebemos","beben","comprendo","comprendes","comprende","comprendemos","comprenden","corro","corres","corre","corremos","corren","creo","crees","cree","creemos","creen","debo","debes","debe","debemos","deben","leo","lees","lee","leemos","leen","vendo","vendes","vende","vendemos","venden","abro","abres","abre","abrimos","abren","comparto","compartes","comparte","compartimos","comparten","escribo","escribes","escribe","escribimos","escriben","recibo","recibes","recibe","recibimos","reciben","asisto","asistes","asiste","asistimos","asisten","decido","decides","decide","decidimos","deciden","describo","describe","describimos","describen","rompo","rompe","barro","barre","sufro","sufre","subo","sube","subimos","suben"]},{"t":"A **nosotros** form (-emos / -imos)","re":"\\b\\p{L}+(emos|imos)\\b"}]},"reflect":{"q":"Don Quijote read so many stories that they changed the way he saw the world. What book, story, show or song has changed the way *you* see something? What did it help you notice?","placeholder":"A story that changed how I see things is…"},"further":{"id":"x1","type":"translate","title":"Challenge: translate","items":[{"en":"We live in Pennsylvania.","es":["[nosotros] vivimos en pensilvania","[nosotras] vivimos en pensilvania"]},{"en":"You (tú) should read more.","es":["[tú] debes leer más"]},{"en":"I'm learning to swim.","es":["[yo] aprendo a nadar"]},{"en":"They share a room.","es":["[ellos] comparten un cuarto","[ellas] comparten un cuarto","[ellos] comparten una habitación","[ellas] comparten una habitación"]}],"hints":["*Learning to* = **aprender a** + infinitive."]},"culture":"**¿Sabías?** On the windy plains of La Mancha you can still see rows of white windmills like the ones Don Quijote attacked, in towns such as **Campo de Criptana** and **Consuegra**.","unitTitle":"Mi vida diaria: el presente","code":"NTA2MS1FVE9KSVVR","prev":"m11-verbos-ar.html","next":"m13-preguntas.html"});
